    <summary>Windows-only PowerPoint automation CLI - requires Microsoft PowerPoint to be installed.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
`pptcli` automates Microsoft PowerPoint from the command line through PowerPoint's
native COM API: create and edit slides, shapes, text, tables, charts, images,
animations and transitions, apply themes, run VBA macros, and export to PDF, images
or video.

### Requirements - read before installing

* **Windows only.** The tool drives PowerPoint through COM interop, which does not
  exist on macOS or Linux. There is no cross-platform build and there cannot be one.
* **Microsoft PowerPoint 2016 or later must already be installed** on the same
  machine. This package does not include PowerPoint and cannot work without it.
* **A desktop session.** `pptcli` controls a real PowerPoint process, so it is not
  suitable for headless or server-side batch processing.
* **.NET 9 Desktop Runtime**, installed automatically as a package dependency.

### Notes

This package ships a framework-dependent build, which is why the .NET 9 Desktop
Runtime is a hard dependency rather than a suggestion.

The same functionality is also available as an MCP server for AI assistants such as
GitHub Copilot and Claude. See the project page for details.
    ]]></description>

    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/trsdn/mcp-server-ppt/releases/tag/v{{VERSION}}</releaseNotes>

    <!--
      Framework-dependent build: the .NET runtime is not bundled. PptMcp.CLI sets
      UseWindowsForms=true, so the base runtime is not enough - it must be the Desktop
      Runtime, or pptcli.exe installs cleanly and then fails to start. Load-bearing.
    -->
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="dotnet-9.0-desktopruntime" version="9.0.0" />
    </dependencies>
